Subject: [PATCH] fix: map feedback command to setup skill

---
 .agents/skills/setup/SKILL.md | 9 +++++++++
 skills/coverage.json          | 1 +
 skills/setup/SKILL.md         | 9 +++++++++
 3 files changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/.agents/skills/setup/SKILL.md b/.agents/skills/setup/SKILL.md
index d9cc02d2..c61daea8 100644
--- a/.agents/skills/setup/SKILL.md
+++ b/.agents/skills/setup/SKILL.md
@@ -40,6 +40,15 @@ forge init --classification standard --dry-run       # preview the adoption conf
 
 `forge init` writes the Forge adoption config (`.forge/config.yaml`). The profile picks how much enforcement ships on: `minimal` (rails off) → `standard` → `full`. This configures the workflow; toggling an individual gate afterward is the **gates** skill.
 
+# Feedback consent
+
+```bash
+forge feedback          # inspect pending privacy-safe reports and consent state
+forge feedback disable  # opt out and delete queued drafts plus the anonymous ID
+```
+
+Feedback defaults off and sends only after the exact structured payload is previewed and approved. Non-interactive use never prompts or sends.
+
 # Diagnose
 
 ```bash
